Package: BOHR
Type: Package
Title: Beta One-Zero Hybrid Regression for Proportions with Exact Zeros and Ones
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yuhao", "Dong", email = "yuhaodong999@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Boxiang", "Liu", role = "aut"))
Description: Regression for proportion data in [0, 1] that contain exact zeros
    and ones, such as the relative usage of a promoter or isoform. The response
    is modelled with a zero-and-one-inflated beta distribution (Ospina and
    Ferrari (2010) <doi:10.1007/s00362-008-0125-4>), and a predictor's effect
    is tested separately on the probability of zero, the probability of one and
    the mean of the values in between. The mean is tested with a small-sample
    corrected likelihood-ratio test of a beta regression (Ferrari and
    Cribari-Neto (2004) <doi:10.1080/0266476042000214501>) and the boundary
    components with Firth-penalised likelihood-ratio tests (Firth (1993)
    <doi:10.1093/biomet/80.1.27>). A genomics layer maps quantitative trait
    loci of alternative promoter usage, with the Cauchy combination test (Liu
    and Xie (2020) <doi:10.1080/01621459.2018.1554485>) and false-discovery
    control. Written in base R.
